        <li>No panic and no rushed decisions, just consistency over years</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>The habit proactive guys are building</h2>
  <p>None of this requires a prescription or a dramatic intervention. For men who want to get ahead of a genetic risk, the starting point is usually nutritional: a small set of herbs and plant extracts that have been studied for their role in supporting healthy DHT balance and normal hair growth. The name that comes up most often is <strong>saw palmetto</strong>, a palm berry extract with a long history of use, typically alongside stinging nettle and other botanicals.</p>

  <figure class="vy-figure">
    <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-384-simply-revival/images/barber-check.jpg" alt="A barber examining the crown of a young client's hair" width="1400" height="900" style="object-position:center 40%">
    <figcaption>The proactive ones treat it like any other checkup: ask your barber once in a while, and build the habit before you need it.</figcaption>
  </figure>
